2. Known issue:
The highest-ranked grasp candidate is consistently feasible and supports
successful E2E execution, while many subsequent GPD candidates are rejected
by CuRobo at the exact-grasp stage with IK_FAIL / no reachable grasp.


3. FeelAnyForce remaining issue:
Dual-side GelSight Mini tactile sensing and FeelAnyForce inference were successfully integrated into the Franka pick-and-place pipeline. Repeated tests confirmed stable tactile acquisition and online inference. However, FeelAnyForce force magnitudes did not consistently agree with Isaac Sim rigid-body contact-force references. Consequently, force predictions remain uncalibrated and are currently used only as observational evidence, not for closed-loop control or calibrated physical reasoning.
